## Section 1 - Subscribers & Growth

Publication: Mastering Observability (`pub_51d69527...`). Full detail: `05_Weekly_Beehiiv_Reports/Beehiiv_Report_2026-08-17.md`.

| Metric (last 4 weeks) | This run | 08-10 | 08-03 | 08-01 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Active subscribers | **558** | 557 | 555 | 557 |
| Open rate | **35.46%** | 31.69% | 37.37% | 38.42% |
| Click rate | **5.19%** | 4.65% | 3.73% | 4.13% |
| New subscribers | 7 | 7 | 10 | 10 |
| Churned | 4 | 4 | 5 | 3 |
| Net subscribers | **+3** | +3 | +5 | +7 |
| Earnings | $6.10 | $6.10 | $6.10 | $6.10 |

**The open-rate collapse reversed.** 31.69% to 35.46%, a 3.77 point recovery that claws back two thirds of last week's 5.68 point fall. The three-run decline (38.42, 37.37, 31.69) did not become a four-run decline. Click rate rose again to 5.19%, the highest reading in this log. Read together: the 08-10 drop looks like send-volume dilution from a three-send week rather than content failure, which is what last run's most-likely reading said. Do not treat this as solved, treat it as evidence that cadence, not quality, moves this number.

Net growth flat at +3 for the second run (7 new, 4 churned). Subscriber count 558, an all-time high for this log by one.

**New subscribers by acquisition source (4wk):** recommendation 7wdata.beehiiv.com 3, website direct 2, recommendation www.project-overwatch.com 1, embed direct 1. Sums cleanly to 7.

**LinkedIn contributed ZERO signups this run.** It led with 5 of 10 two runs ago, fell to 2 of 7 last run, and is now 0 of 7. The **beehiiv recommendation network is now 4 of 7 (57%)** and has added a second referring publication (project-overwatch). This matters because LinkedIn traffic did not fall: on-site referrals from LinkedIn actually **rose** from 46 to 56 sessions. So the channel Allan actively works is sending more people and converting none of them, while a passive channel he does not touch is doing all the acquiring. That is a landing-page problem, not a reach problem.

**Published posts: 137** (was 134). Three new since the last run: "Lead with the promise, not the plumbing" (08-10), "What Are Wide Events? Observability 2.0, Without the Hype" (08-13, the TT04 written anchor), "Own the Signal, Rent the Platform" (08-16).

**Signal Drop pages: 23 tagged `signal_drop`, minus the still-live duplicate = 22 unique live episode pages** against a target of 17. No new Signal Drop this period. **Carried flag:** the duplicate "Your Role Changes Every Hour" (`post_0cbfa4e6` plus `post_47600cdf`) is still live on both IDs, **fourth run flagged**.

## Section 2 - Website & SEO Traffic

**Beehiiv website analytics (4wk vs prior 4wk):** unique visitors 188 (+8.7%), sessions 284 (+20.9%), page views 545 (-2.9%), bounce rate 48.59% (worse), avg session duration 72.03s (-52.1%).

**More people, more sessions, and they are leaving faster than at any point in this log.** Bounce rate has now worsened four runs running: 38.22, 41.45, 44.59, **48.59**. Session duration fell from 111.3s last run to 72.03s, a 35% drop. Traffic is up and attention is down. Combined with the LinkedIn-traffic-without-LinkedIn-signups finding above, the site is now getting a materially worse conversion outcome per visitor than it was a month ago.

**Top pages by page views:** / (144), poll results page (30), Ep25 Gate Stays Human podcast (30), /p/observability-maturity-assessment (25), /metrics-and-mayhem/book (23), /metrics-and-mayhem/free-chapter (22), /products/metrics-mayhem-chapter-4 (18), /metrics-and-mayhem/podcast (17), /p/quiet-isnt-good (16), **/advisory (15)**, /subscribe (15), /p/lead-with-the-promise (15), /p/what-is-opentelemetry-profiling (15), /p/how-to-lead-an-incident-response-team (15), /p/observability-digest-july-2026 (13), TT02 (10). Note: /p/what-is-a-wide-event only 5 page views since 08-13 publish.

**Top referrers (sessions):** Direct 172, linkedin.com 33, LinkedIn Android 23, google.com 19, self-referral 8, beehiiv.com 7, reddit.com 5, ecosia 3, **substack.com 3 (new)**, facebook.com 2, static.microsoft 2, Gmail Android 1, google.de 1, t.co 1, cto.academy 1, youtube.com 1, bing.com 1.

**Google Search Console: read live this run.** Full detail: `06_Search_Console_Reports/GSC_Report_2026-08-17.md`.

**Site totals (rolling 3 months, 16 May to 15 Aug 2026): 53 clicks, 5,950 impressions, 0.9% CTR, average position 27.3, 286 queries.** Against 08-10 (51 / 5,990 / 0.9% / 26.7 / 272) and baseline (49 / 9,880 / 0.5% / 19.5). Clicks up 2, impressions flat, position drifted 0.6 further out, query count up another 14. The pattern of the last month holds: the surface keeps widening (254, 272, 286 queries) while total impression volume stays flat and average position slowly worsens. That is what happens when a site starts ranking for many new terms at poor positions.

**Top queries:** grafana alloy (**1 click** / 65 impr / 1.5% / pos 25.0), sunny mattu (1 / 35 / 2.9% / 6.6), **observability maturity assessment (1 / 5 / 20% / 16.2, NEW)**, opentelemetry collector (0 / 222 / 69.9), hybrid cloud operations (0 / 153 / 49.9), observability cost (0 / 139 / 27.4), signal drop (0 / 124 / **5.4**), what is grafana alloy (0 / 99 / **10.7**), observability vs monitoring (0 / 95 / 46.8), observability news (0 / 74 / 48.1).

Keyword movement against the plan's targets:

- **"observability maturity assessment" is new and already converting.** 1 click on 5 impressions is a 20% CTR, the best on the site. The blog published 08-09 is indexed and matching its target term inside eight days. This is the clearest evidence yet that the assessment content line works as an SEO play, and it is a commercial-intent term.
- **"grafana alloy" returned to the top ten with a click** (65 impressions, position 25.0) after dropping out entirely last run.
- **"what is grafana alloy" improved 10.8 to 10.7** and impressions jumped 69 to 99, but it is a fourth consecutive read just off page one with zero clicks.
- **"signal drop" improved 5.6 to 5.4** and remains the largest wasted page-one position on the site: 124 impressions, 0 clicks, three runs running.

**Top pages by clicks:** / (18 / 136 / 13.2% / 6.2), **/authors/allan-mann (11 / 47 / 23.4% / 6.9)**, /metrics-and-mayhem/podcast (7 / 112 / 6.2% / 5.6), /p/what-is-grafana-alloy (3 / **683** / 0.4% / 13.3), **/authors/67e0a785-... (3 / 22 / 13.6% / 5.5)**, /p/sunny-mattu-capgemini (2 / 67 / 3% / 7.5), /t/observability (1 / 70 / 1.4% / 23.4), /t/observability_digest (1 / 47 / 2.1% / 6.4), /subscribe (1 / 40 / 2.5% / 5.3), Signal Drop Accountability Is the Job (1 / 37 / 2.7% / 11.9).

**The author-page finding holds, second run.** The two author pages produce **14 of 53 organic clicks (26%)** at 23.4% and 13.6% CTR. They are still the best-converting surface on the site, still a duplicate splitting one intent, and still route nowhere. Nothing has changed since it was flagged on 08-10.

**Biggest impression sink:** /p/what-is-grafana-alloy at 683 impressions for 3 clicks (0.4% CTR, position 13.3), 11% of all site impressions. The cost-strategy post that was the other half of last run's pair (732 impressions) has dropped out of the top ten pages entirely.

## Section 3 - Lead Magnets & Funnel (SEO-to-Revenue)

Per `05_SEO_TO_REVENUE_MODEL.md`: SEO has two jobs, feed advisory and grow the newsletter.

| Signal | Organic (GSC) | On-site (4wk) | Move vs 08-10 |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Free-chapter** | 0 clicks / **3 impressions** / pos **36.7** | 22 page views | Impressions 2 to 3, position 39.5 to 36.7. Both improving. On-site **35 to 22, down 37%**. |
| **Advisory** | 0 clicks / **19 impressions** / pos **7.6** | 15 page views | Impressions 12 to 19 (+58%), **position 10.2 to 7.6, back onto page one**. On-site 24 to 15, down 38%. |
| **Newsletter signups by source** | n/a | 7 new subs | **LinkedIn 2 to 0. Recommendation network 3 to 4 of 7.** |

**The advisory page is the headline of this run.** Three consecutive reads: 5 impressions at position 7.2, then 12 at 10.2, now **19 at 7.6**. Impressions have nearly quadrupled in a fortnight and the page is back inside page one. It still returns zero clicks. Its two ranking queries are "allan mann" (position 9.0) and **"observability in banking" (position 50.0)**, which is worth noting against Section 6 below: the regulated-industry angle is showing up in Allan's own search data.

A page at position 7.6 with 19 impressions and 0 clicks is a title and snippet problem, not a ranking problem. This is the same recommendation as last run, now with a stronger case: the lever got better, and it was not pulled.

**The counter-signal is louder this run.** On-site views for the money pages fell again: free-chapter 35 to 22, advisory 24 to 15. Only /book rose (20 to 23). Meanwhile total sessions rose 21% and bounce rate hit an all-time worst. More visitors, fewer of them reaching the commercial pages.

**3b - extended lead-magnet map:**

- **/products/metrics-mayhem-chapter-4:** 18 page views (was 20). GSC 0 clicks / 0 impressions, confirmed by exact-URL filter. Live "Lead magnet automation" (`purchased_product`) unchanged at 8 enrolled / 8 completed / 12.5% open / **0% click**. It delivers, it gets read occasionally, it converts nobody. Watch item, not a leak.
- **/metrics-and-mayhem/book:** 23 page views (was 20), the only money page that grew. GSC 0/0. No dedicated beehiiv automation, expected (external purchase route).
- **/metrics-and-mayhem/free-chapter:** 22 page views, 3 GSC impressions. **Still no dedicated nurture automation in the account. This remains the one true funnel leak in the map.** GR-13-02 (ungate /free-chapter) remains open, now more urgent: the page has surfaced organically for two consecutive runs and its position is improving.
- **Author pages:** still not in the lead-magnet map, still producing 26% of organic clicks, still no CTA. Second run recommending they be added.

